WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:06.870
Evan wrote in, Evan says, Hey David, when
do you think Tulsi is going to take Elizabeth

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.140
Warren down?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.020
Listen, it's not gonna happen.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.020
Okay.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:18.599
And I, the, the conversation we've talked
enough about Tulsi Gabbert and other candidates

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:22.060
that have these sort of cults of personality
around them.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.619
I don't even really listen.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:29.569
If you, if you literally believe that at some
point in the future in the 2020 primary, you

00:00:29.569 --> 00:00:34.220
will look at the polls and Tulsi Gabard will
be ahead of Elizabeth Warren.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.960
I probably can't talk you out of that belief.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.900
You're probably ideologically committed to
that belief regardless of what the facts are

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.500
about the way that this primary is going.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.800
So I don't even want to argue about that.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.060
What I want to think about is when the Tulsi
people or the yang people, cause I, I hear

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.830
this from both the Tulsi people in the yang
people.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.760
This is an honest question for you guys.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:03.440
When you write into me and you say, David,
the poles, I don't care what they say soon

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.909
Andrew Yang will be in the lead or soon Tulsi
Gabard will be in the lead.

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:15.480
Do you literally believe that or is it something
you say to keep up the momentum and the energy

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.230
and to try to energize the supporters?

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:22.870
I genuinely want to know the answer to that
because if people really literally are sitting

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:30.210
around saying, I don't care that Tulsi Gavin's
pulling 0.8% any day, now all of a sudden

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.780
she's going to surge.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:38.620
Whether it was her threat to boy, her pre
debate threat to boycott the debate or whether

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.010
it's her performance in a debate or whatever.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:46.730
What is it that you believe is going to happen
in the minds of the American people that they

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:53.190
will see her and say, you know what, I, I
now realize I have to support Tulsi Gabbert.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.690
What are, what are the mechanics that you
think are going to lead to that?

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.550
And if it's just something that you're saying
in order to keep people energized or keep

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.299
the energy up, I, that's fine.

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:04.190
I would actually respect you much more if
you wrote to me and you said, you know what

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:09.200
David, I do go around online posting on YouTube
videos including yours or those of others.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.200
Tulsi is eventually going to take over.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.910
Yang is eventually going to take over the
lead.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.340
I don't actually believe it.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.530
I'm just being positive.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.640
I would respect that sincerely.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.880
Uh, but if you are actually waiting around
for the day that you believe is coming where

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.780
they will be in the lead of the democratic
primary, I want to figure out exactly what

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.960
it is that you're thinking.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.840
And I do think that this relates to the very
counterproductive cults of personality, personality

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:38.230
around some of these candidates that I don't
really get what the end game is.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:44.901
And I know that eventually when these candidates
don't win and drop out or just lose a, you

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:50.020
will then come forward and have some other
kind of motivated reasoning to explain who

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:57.140
screwed them or what conspiracy led to them
not winning, even though they otherwise would

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.140
have.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:03.280
And it'll be a, you know, endless, endless,
motivated reasoning along those lines.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.410
I want some of you to get in touch and say,
you know what, David, I don't believe that

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.520
they're going to win.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.590
It's just something I go around saying because
it either makes me feel good or it makes other

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:12.590
people feel good.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:13.060
I'd respect you for telling me that

